    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d850">

                <pb facs="1301" n="1275" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v16/pg1275"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">751G.00/7–254: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Embassy in
                        France</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d850-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1954-07-02T19:34:00-04:00">July 2, 1954—7:34
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>39. ReDeptel 4852, June 28; Saigon 2746; Geneva 489.<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d850-f2"/> It seems to me that new Vietnamese Prime Minister Ngo
                    Dinh Diem, who has reputation of uncompromising nationalist, is quite in the
                    dark about developments critically affecting country he is trying to lead. We
                    fear that if results of French negotiations with Communists are revealed to him
                    as a <hi rendition="#italic">fait accompli</hi>, the very reaction French wish
                    to avoid will result.</p>
                <p>You should therefore indicate our concern to the French and ascertain their own
                    intentions with respect to consulting him or minimizing his resentment and their
                    views with respect to plans and prospects for maintaining order in South
                    Vietnam.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dulles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d850-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d850-f1-content">
                <p>Drafted by Gullion of S/P and by Sturm of FE. Repeated to Saigon as telegram 31
                    and to Geneva as telegram 9.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d850-f2" n="2" xml:id="d850-f2-content">
                <p>Dated June 28, <ref target="#pg1257">p. 1257</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
